HOW IT WORKS

Every initiative is tagged to the guideline objectives it serves. An initiative
can serve more than one — a dashboard removes manual work and is also a
dashboard delivered — so it is tagged to both.

The important part is that each objective is measured in a different unit, so
nothing is ever counted twice:

  Objective 1  Financial              a return, in per cent
  Objective 2  F&A process automation saving hours
  Objective 3  F&A Data warehouse     a delivery date
  Objective 4  Efficiency             number of dashboards delivered
  Objective 5  Automation E2E, AI     number of E2E / AI solutions delivered

Objective 2 collects the saving hours of every initiative in the plan, whatever
else that initiative is tagged to. It is the only objective counted in hours.
Objectives 4 and 5 count what was delivered, not the hours behind it, because
those hours are already in Objective 2. Objective 1 puts a price on the same
hours and asks whether the effort was worth it.

That is why a dashboard saving 8 hours a month adds 8 hours to Objective 2 and
one dashboard to Objective 4, and the team total does not move.

OBJECTIVE 1 — A RETURN, NOT AN AMOUNT

I have set Objective 1 as a floor rather than a baht amount: the overall return
must be at least 200%. A baht target can be met simply by doing more work,
which does not answer the question the guideline asks. A return does.

It is calculated per initiative and rolled up:

  Benefit     saving hours x the blended user rate, over a year
              plus any cash saving stated on the initiative
  Investment  development mandays x the developer rate
              plus any hardware or licence cost, plus running cost

  Return      (benefit over 12 months - investment) / investment

The figure recalculates the moment anything behind it changes, so the plan
always shows where we actually stand rather than a number typed in once.

COST ASSUMPTIONS

From the Man-hour rate_IT_Tech.xlsx you shared:

  Developer, junior/mid   THB 3,200 per manday   development investment
  Staff                   THB 1,700 per manday   user-side benefit
  Manager                 THB 6,500 per manday   user-side benefit

Saving hours come from both staff and managers, so I used a blended mix of 20%
manager and 80% staff over 22 working days a month:

  Manager   20% x 3,200 x 22 = THB 28,600
  Staff     80% x 1,700 x 22 = THB 29,920
  Blended                      THB 58,520 a month

An initiative needing 20 development mandays is therefore an investment of THB
64,000, before any hardware, licence or running cost.

Every rate above is adjustable in the tool, so the whole plan can be repriced
if you would prefer different assumptions.

